# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds the MySQL password and any search-provider API keys. .env.example
# is committed instead, so a fresh clone knows what to set without ever having
# the real values in history — where they would be permanent even after deletion.
.env
.env.local

# ── generated code graph ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rebuilt from the syntax trees after every commit by tools/graphify/graphify.py, so it is
# derived data with a source of truth already in the repository. Committing it would create
# a conflict on almost every merge, and a stale copy in history is worse than none because
# it still looks authoritative.
.graphify/

# ── local data, never shared ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SQLite call history and the ephemeral live-progress files. Machine-specific
# and regenerated on demand; committing them would also commit every prompt and
# response ever recorded.
.local-llm-data/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Node / Next.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright UI verification output: screenshots of the running dashboard.
.ui-check/

# ── editors and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── local-only tooling: graphify and Obsidian ──
# graphify is development infrastructure that lives outside every repository, in
# Ideas/.tools/graphify, and writes its graphs to Ideas/.graphify/<project>/. Nothing about
# it belongs in a project's history: the tool is shared and versionless by choice, and the
# graph is derived data whose source of truth is the code beside it. A committed graph would
# conflict on nearly every merge, and a stale one in history still looks authoritative.
#
# These entries are defensive. The output already lives outside the repo, so in normal use
# none of them match anything — they exist so that a copy landing in the working tree by
# accident, or an older layout, cannot be committed.
.graphify/
graphify-out/
tools/graphify/
.claude/skills/graphify/

# Obsidian's own workspace state: per-machine UI layout, plugin settings and caches. It has
# no meaning on another computer and changes every time the app is opened.
.obsidian/
